Hi Lukas

Well spotted! Indeed the output is a confidence interval, not the se. I will update this later on, either changing the doc or the function. So stay updated. I've opened an github issue <https://github.com/MatthieuStigler/tsDyn/issues/13> for that.

Also, note that there is a new published paper describing tsDyn link <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0169716119300355>, I would appreciate if you can refer to this one for citation purpose.

Best,
Matthieu

